---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const post = {
  title: 'Team Collaboration Best Practices for WATeamInbox',
  date: 'January 2, 2026',
  readTime: '6 min read',
  category: 'Guide',
  author: 'WATeamInbox Team'
};
---

<Layout title={`${post.title} - WATeamInbox Blog`}>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-24 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="text-center">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-3">
        <span class="rounded-full bg-emerald-100 px-3 py-1 text-sm font-medium text-emerald-800">
          {post.category}
        </span>
        <span class="text-gray-500">{post.readTime}</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900 md:text-5xl" data-testid="blog-post-title">
        {post.title}
      </h1>
      <div class="mt-6 flex items-center justify-center gap-4 text-gray-600">
        <span>By {post.author}</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <time>{post.date}</time>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Featured Image -->
    <div class="mt-12 flex h-64 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-600 to-emerald-800 md:h-96">
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-32 w-32 text-white/60" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.5" d="M17 20h5v-2a3 3 0 00-5.356-1.857M17 20H7m10 0v-2c0-.656-.126-1.283-.356-1.857M7 20H2v-2a3 3 0 015.356-1.857M7 20v-2c0-.656.126-1.283.356-1.857m0 0a5.002 5.002 0 019.288 0M15 7a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0zm6 3a2 2 0 11-4 0 2 2 0 014 0zM7 10a2 2 0 11-4 0 2 2 0 014 0z" />
      </svg>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="prose prose-lg mx-auto mt-12 max-w-3xl" data-testid="blog-post-content">
      <p class="lead text-xl text-gray-600">
        Effective team collaboration is essential for delivering exceptional customer experiences on WhatsApp. This guide covers proven strategies for managing team workflows, contact assignments, and communication best practices.
      </p>

      <h2>Understanding Roles and Permissions</h2>
      <p>
        WATeamInbox offers a permission system with three primary roles, each designed for different responsibilities:
      </p>

      <div class="rounded-lg bg-gray-50 p-6 not-prose my-8">
        <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">Role Hierarchy</h4>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
            <div class="flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-purple-100">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5 text-purple-600" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.042-.133-2.052-.382-3.016z" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h5 class="font-medium text-gray-900">Owner</h5>
              <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Full access including team management, billing, and all permissions. Cannot be removed or demoted.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
            <div class="flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-100">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5 text-blue-600" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10.325 4.317c.426-1.756 2.924-1.756 3.35 0a1.724 1.724 0 002.573 1.066c1.543-.94 3.31.826 2.37 2.37a1.724 1.724 0 001.065 2.572c1.756.426 1.756 2.924 0 3.35a1.724 1.724 0 00-1.066 2.573c.94 1.543-.826 3.31-2.37 2.37a1.724 1.724 0 00-2.572 1.065c-.426 1.756-2.924 1.756-3.35 0a1.724 1.724 0 00-2.573-1.066c-1.543.94-3.31-.826-2.37-2.37a1.724 1.724 0 00-1.065-2.572c-1.756-.426-1.756-2.924 0-3.35a1.724 1.724 0 001.066-2.573c-.94-1.543.826-3.31 2.37-2.37.996.608 2.296.07 2.572-1.065z" />
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 12a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0z" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h5 class="font-medium text-gray-900">Admin</h5>
              <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Can invite team members, assign contacts, view all chats, export data, and manage most settings.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
            <div class="flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-gray-100">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5 text-gray-600" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M16 7a4 4 0 11-8 0 4 4 0 018 0zM12 14a7 7 0 00-7 7h14a7 7 0 00-7-7z" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h5 class="font-medium text-gray-900">Member</h5>
              <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Can send messages and manage their assigned contacts. Limited visibility based on assignments.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Contact Assignment Strategies</h2>
      <p>
        Proper contact assignment ensures no customer falls through the cracks and everyone knows who's responsible for what.
      </p>

      <h3>Auto-Assignment on First Reply</h3>
      <p>
        When a team member sends the first message to an unassigned contact, that contact is automatically assigned to them. This creates natural ownership and accountability.
      </p>

      <h3>Manual Assignment for Specialized Cases</h3>
      <p>
        For complex cases or when a contact needs specific expertise, admins can manually assign contacts to the most suitable team member.
      </p>

      <h3>Takeover with Notification</h3>
      <p>
        When reassigning a contact from one team member to another, the previous owner receives a notification. This ensures smooth handoffs and prevents confusion.
      </p>

      <h2>Communication Best Practices</h2>

      <h3>Use Private Notes for Internal Context</h3>
      <p>
        Private notes are only visible to you, making them perfect for personal reminders about a contact. Use them for:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Personal observations about customer preferences</li>
        <li>Internal notes about ongoing issues</li>
        <li>Reminders for follow-up actions</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Use Shared Notes for Team Context</h3>
      <p>
        Shared notes are visible to all team members, ensuring everyone has the same information:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Customer history and previous interactions</li>
        <li>Important account details</li>
        <li>Special instructions or preferences</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Leverage Quick Replies</h3>
      <p>
        Create quick reply templates for common responses. This ensures consistency and saves time:
      </p>

      <div class="rounded-lg bg-gray-50 p-6 not-prose my-8">
        <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">Example Quick Replies</h4>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <div class="rounded border border-gray-200 bg-white p-3">
            <code class="text-sm text-primary-600">/greeting</code>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600">Hello! Thank you for reaching out to [Company]. How can I help you today?</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded border border-gray-200 bg-white p-3">
            <code class="text-sm text-primary-600">/hours</code>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600">Our business hours are Monday-Friday, 9 AM - 6 PM. We'll respond to your message as soon as we're back!</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded border border-gray-200 bg-white p-3">
            <code class="text-sm text-primary-600">/thanks</code>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600">Thank you for choosing [Company]! If you have any other questions, don't hesitate to ask.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Monitoring and Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        Use the dashboard to monitor team performance and identify areas for improvement:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Response Time</strong> - Track how quickly your team responds to messages</li>
        <li><strong>Resolution Rate</strong> - Monitor how many conversations are being resolved</li>
        <li><strong>Engagement Score</strong> - Measure overall customer engagement quality</li>
        <li><strong>Team Activity</strong> - See who's handling the most conversations</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Audit Logging for Accountability</h2>
      <p>
        WATeamInbox records supported workspace actions in its audit log. Use it to:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Track message history and who sent what</li>
        <li>Monitor contact assignment changes</li>
        <li>Review permission modifications</li>
        <li>Export logs for internal review</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Keyboard Shortcuts for Efficiency</h2>
      <p>
        Train your team on keyboard shortcuts to improve productivity:
      </p>

      <div class="rounded-lg bg-gray-50 p-6 not-prose my-8">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4">
          <div>
            <code class="rounded bg-gray-200 px-2 py-1 text-sm">Ctrl/Cmd + N</code>
            <span class="ml-2 text-sm text-gray-600">New chat</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <code class="rounded bg-gray-200 px-2 py-1 text-sm">Ctrl/Cmd + F</code>
            <span class="ml-2 text-sm text-gray-600">Search</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <code class="rounded bg-gray-200 px-2 py-1 text-sm">Enter</code>
            <span class="ml-2 text-sm text-gray-600">Send message</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <code class="rounded bg-gray-200 px-2 py-1 text-sm">Shift + Enter</code>
            <span class="ml-2 text-sm text-gray-600">New line</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <code class="rounded bg-gray-200 px-2 py-1 text-sm">Escape</code>
            <span class="ml-2 text-sm text-gray-600">Close panel</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <code class="rounded bg-gray-200 px-2 py-1 text-sm">Ctrl/Cmd + /</code>
            <span class="ml-2 text-sm text-gray-600">Show shortcuts</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Conclusion</h2>
      <p>
        Effective collaboration in WATeamInbox requires clear roles, smart assignment strategies, and consistent communication practices. These habits can help teams work efficiently and maintain accountability.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Author Bio -->
    <div class="mt-16 border-t border-gray-200 pt-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
        <div class="flex h-16 w-16 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-100">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-8 w-8 text-emerald-600" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M16 7a4 4 0 11-8 0 4 4 0 018 0zM12 14a7 7 0 00-7 7h14a7 7 0 00-7-7z" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900">{post.author}</p>
          <p class="text-gray-600">Building the future of business communication.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Back to Blog -->
    <div class="mt-12 text-center">
      <a href="/blog" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-primary-600 hover:text-primary-700">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" />
        </svg>
        Back to Blog
      </a>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
